    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0695" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/773: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-05T15:00:00-05:00">November 5, 1919—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3675. Confidential for Polk from the Secretary. Phillips has shown me your 4958.
                    I really think that it would be best for you to return on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">George Washington</hi> if it is possible for you to do
                    so. I appreciate that there are many important problems which you are handling
                    in Paris but I think that many of these could now properly be transferred to the
                    State Department. From here you will have even a stronger position in handling
                    these problems. The <hi rendition="#italic">George Washington</hi> is about to
                    be transferred to the War Department which plans to keep her in the
                    Trans-Atlantic service temporarily.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
